    "title": "2026 Masters Saturday channel: TV schedule for Round 3 at Augusta National",
    "text": "Hoping to watch the 2026 Masters on TV Saturday? We've got you covered.Getty ImagesThe 2026 Masters continues on Saturday with Round 3 at Augusta National. CBS will provide TV coverage of all the third-round action, but there are plenty of other opporunities to watch as well. Keep reading for a complete 2026 Masters Saturday TV schedule and streaming information.What channel is Masters Round 3 on?ESPN aired TV coverage for Thursday’s opening round and Friday’s second round, but for Saturday’s third round, coverage will switch to the Masters longtime TV home: CBS.AdvertisementCBS’ Masters Saturday broadcast will start at 2 p.m. ET and last five hours, finishing at 7 p.m. ET. But there’s even more Masters coverage available online.As they did last year, Paramount+ will provide two hours of early Saturday streaming coverage beginning at 12 p.m. ET. You can also watch the early coverage for free on Masers.com and the Masters App.Additional viewing optiong will be provided online via Masters.com, the Masters App, Paramount+, the ESPN App and more, including featured group and featured hole coverage.Below you will find more detailed information on how to watch the third round of the 2026 Masters.AdvertisementMasters Saturday TV scheduleCBS will air Saturday’s third round of the 2026 Masters on TV from 2-7 p.m. ET.Masters Saturday streaming scheduleYou can stream Saturday’s third round of the 2026 Masters online on Masters.com, the Masters app, the ESPN App, Amazon Prime Video, Paramount+ and DirecTV.Here’s the full Masters streaming schedule for Saturday:On the Range: 10 a.m.-12 p.m. (Masters.com, Masters App, Paramount+)Featured Groups: 10:15 a.m.-7 p.m. (Masters.com, Masters App, Paramount+, Prime Video, ESPN App, DirecTV)Featured Holes (4, 5 and 6): 10:30 a.m.-3:30 p.m. (Masters.com, Masters App, ESPN App)Featured Holes (Amen Corner, 11, 12 and 13): 11:45 a.m.-6 p.m. (Masters.com, Masters App, Paramount+, Prime Video, ESPN App, DirecTV)Featured Holes (15 and 16): 11:45 a.m.-7 p.m. (Masters.com, Masters App, Paramount+, Prime Video, ESPN App, DirecTV)Round 3 Early Coverage: 12-2 p.m. (Paramount+)Round 3 CBS Telecast: 2-7 p.m. (Paramount+)Full Round 3 Stream: 12-7 p.m. (Masters.com, Masters App)Advertisement2026 Masters Saturday tee times (All times ET)Tee No. 19:31 a.m. – Kurt Kitayama, Alex Noren9:42 a.m. – Charl Schwartzel, Rasmus Højgaard9:53 a.m. – Jon Rahm, Si Woo Kim10:04 a.m. – Brian Harman, Corey Conners10:15 a.m. – Sergio Garcia, Maverick McNealy10:26 a.m. – Keegan Bradley, Viktor Hovland10:37 a.m. – Justin Thomas, Gary Woodland10:48 a.m. – Samuel Stevens, Adam Scott11:10 a.m. – Marco Penge, Matt McCarty11:21 a.m. – Jordan Spieth, Sepp Straka11:32 a.m. – Aaron Rai, Jacob Bridgeman11:43 a.m. – Patrick Cantlay, Sungjae Im11:54 a.m. – Dustin Johnson, Russell Henley12:05 p.m. – Harris English, Ryan Gerard12:16 p.m. – Ludvig Åberg, Scottie Scheffler12:38 p.m. – Collin Morikawa, Brian Campbell12:49 p.m. – Nick Taylor, Matt Fitzpatrick1:00 p.m. – Hideki Matsuyama, Michael Brennan1:11 p.m. – Jake Knapp, Xander Schauffele1:22 p.m. – Ben Griffin, Max Homa1:33 p.m. – Chris Gotterup, Brooks Koepka1:55 p.m. – Jason Day, Cameron Young2:06 p.m. – Haotong Li, Kristoffer Reitan2:17 p.m. – Wyndham Clark, Tyrrell Hatton2:28 p.m. – Shane Lowry, Tommy Fleetwood2:39 p.m. – Patrick Reed, Justin Rose2:50 p.m. – Rory McIlroy, Sam BurnsThe post 2026 Masters Saturday channel: TV schedule for Round 3 at Augusta National appeared first on Golf.",
